    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 78475,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78475.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "Well, one of the very first things that I'm focused on, of course, is the security and safety of the people of the state, and that's why we're going to make sure to gather the National Guard and the adjacent general, of course, the state police, the state fire marshal, and all of the security services of the state, including the emergency management agency, to be prepared for every eventuality. Obviously, there are snow emergencies, tornadoes, And then, of course, the danger and risk potentially of any national security threats we need to be prepared for. So that's going to be day one to make sure that we've got that covered. And then, of course, the regular operation of each of those agencies I want to make sure is smooth.",
