  },
  {
    "episode_id": 78475,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78475.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'm excited to celebrate the 200th anniversary of our state. You know, we've had such a tremendous history of success. We're the land of Abraham Lincoln and Barack Obama of Ronald Reagan and Ulysses S. Grant were a state that's created so many products and services and jobs over many years and companies have emanated out of our state that have succeeded worldwide. There's just so much to celebrate and I'm really glad that we're able to do it tonight and especially that we're all coming together. I know that Governor Rauner and I Of course, we'll be there together, but so many others from all walks of life will be joining in on the bicentennial celebration. It's frankly a testament, I think, to who we are as Illinoisans. that were all coming together tonight to have this celebration.",
