  {
    "episode_id": 78475,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78475.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Oh, no. Look, we had a very robust campaign for a year and a half. And the voters have spoken. And I think I'm excited about the prospect of coming together, working across the aisle with Republicans in Springfield. to get the job done. You know, we need to be problem solvers now. The ideology we need to toss out the window, but we need to ask ourselves, you know, how are we going to overcome the challenges of the state? I've put forward some good ideas for doing that, but you know, Republicans have good ideas too. And that's why in my transition, I've invited Republicans to sit together with Democrats to bring those ideas forward. And we're going to make sure that we're addressing those challenges early on in the administration.",
