  {
    "episode_id": 78475,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78475.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Well, as you can imagine, when you put a committee together like the one we announced today, that's focused on a 21st century economy, for example, that you need to have all the voices at the table that are going to participate in that economy. So you want to have a lot of people at the table, but we've broken up each of the committees into subcommittees so that all of the subject areas that fall underneath these are being covered. And I want to make sure that we've got a menu of the best ideas from some of the best experts in the state and that's what you'll see among these committees. These really are people who know their stuff, who can lead and help us make sure that as we move forward that the challenges of balancing the budget and dealing with our pension challenge, creating jobs in the state, lowering the cost of healthcare and the cost of higher education and bringing back vocational training and career and technical education into our high schools. that all of those things are being brought to state government as I take office and then we're able to implement them. The good ideas are here. We don't need to look elsewhere. We've got the best people and the best ideas and the best experts. We just need to finally get the job done by working together and solving real problems.",
