    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "Well, certainly making sure that we're working to raise wages for people across the state. That's the priority. As you know, the General Assembly did pass a raise in the minimum wage last year. It was vetoed by the governor. I want to make sure that we're doing everything we can to address the kitchen table issues that I talked about throughout the campaign, and that includes raising wages And making sure that we're raising standards of living. So I think we can raise the minimum wage in the state. I think we can do it relatively early on in this administration. And I'm going to work hard to do it. And at the same time, for those who are concerned about raising the minimum wage because They think it will raise costs for businesses. Understand that I'm very focused on making sure that we minimize any negative impact that people may feel in small businesses across downstate Illinois, for example. And so we're going to work on that. This isn't just a hike the minimum wage. One day it's going to be $15. We've got to make sure that we're easing it in, that we're raising people's standards of living, but also making sure we're not losing any jobs in the process. And that's one of the reasons why I've made sure that, for example, the retail merchants are at the table at the same time that labor unions are there so that we can put this together in a bipartisan fashion.",
